# Testing Rules

For critical behavior, choose the appropriate level:

Unit:
- validation
- mappers
- utilities
- business rules

Integration:
- services
- forms
- important components
- API interactions

E2E:
- authentication
- critical CRUD flows
- authorization
- search/filter
- language switching (next-intl locale change)

Run checks only when the user asks. Do not open the browser unless they ask:
- TypeScript
- lint
- tests relevant to the change
- build
- loading, error, and empty states
- responsive behavior
- accessibility
- next-intl (keys present, no hardcoded user-visible strings in touched UI)
- regressions
